#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:23
msgid "<a0>Accompanying Clinician from Origin Country</a0>"
msgstr "<a0>来源国随行临床医生</a0>"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:22
msgid "<a0>Counsellor</a0>"
msgstr "<a0>咨询师</a0>"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:24
#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:25
msgid "<a0>Host Country Health Worker</a0>"
msgstr "<a0>东道国卫生工作者</a0>"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:20
msgid "<a0>Pilgrim</a0>"
msgstr "<a0>朝觐者</a0>"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:20
msgid "61, from Kuala Terengganu, Malaysia, performing Hajj for the first time. Has type 2 diabetes and high blood pressure; takes insulin and two tablets a day; allergic to penicillin. Carries one phone."
msgstr "61 岁，来自马来西亚 Kuala Terengganu，首次进行朝觐（Hajj）。患有 2 型糖尿病和高血压；使用胰岛素，每天服用两种药片；对青霉素过敏。携带一部手机。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:21
msgid "Accompanying family member (not yet a persona here)"
msgstr "随行家庭成员（此处尚未作为人物画像）"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:139
msgid "An account of access back to the home country (P5, P7), and of language (P5)."
msgstr "说明如何将访问情况反馈回本国（P5、P7），以及语言问题（P5）。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:27
msgid "And the systems: Kamal's national health wallet (<a0>Origin Country Wallet</a0>), Malaysia's health information exchange (<a1>Origin Country HIE</a1>), the facility's EMR (<a2>Host Country EMR</a2>), and WHO GDHCN, the trust network both countries take part in."
msgstr "以及各系统：Kamal 的国家健康钱包（<a0>来源国钱包</a0>）、马来西亚的健康信息交换（<a1>来源国 HIE</a1>）、医疗机构的 EMR（<a2>东道国 EMR</a2>），以及两国共同参与的信任网络——世卫组织（WHO）GDHCN。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:136
msgid "Business processes for P0 (keys and terminologies), P2 (assembling the IPS) and P6 (break the glass)."
msgstr "P0（密钥和术语）、P2（汇编 IPS）和 P6（紧急破例访问）的业务流程。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:23
msgid "Doctor of the Malaysian Hajj medical team, travelling with the pilgrims."
msgstr "马来西亚朝觐（Hajj）医疗队的医生，随朝觐者同行。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:22
msgid "Dr Aisyah"
msgstr "Dr Aisyah"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:25
msgid "Dr Faisal"
msgstr "Dr Faisal"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:23
msgid "Dr Hafiz"
msgstr "Dr Hafiz"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:25
msgid "Emergency physician at the same facility."
msgstr "同一医疗机构的急诊医生。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:8
msgid "Every person in this story is fictional. The setting follows this guide's <a0>Malaysian reference implementation</a0>: a pilgrim from Malaysia performing Hajj in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia (KSA)."
msgstr "本故事中的所有人物均为虚构。背景沿用本指南的<a0>马来西亚参考实现</a0>：一位来自马来西亚的朝觐者在沙特阿拉伯王国（KSA）进行朝觐（Hajj）。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:140
msgid "Example patients that are pilgrims: today's examples are a resident of the Netherlands."
msgstr "作为朝觐者的示例患者：目前的示例是一位荷兰居民。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:22
msgid "General practitioner in Kuala Terengganu, empanelled by the national pilgrimage authority for pre-Hajj health examinations."
msgstr "Kuala Terengganu 的全科医生，由国家朝觐管理机构委派开展朝觐（Hajj）前健康检查。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:18
msgid "Generic persona"
msgstr "通用人物画像"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:20
msgid "Kamal"
msgstr "Kamal"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:128
msgid "Kamal comes home. His GP in Kuala Terengganu does not know he was treated in Mina."
msgstr "Kamal 回到家中。他在 Kuala Terengganu 的全科医生（GP）并不知道他曾在米纳（Mina）接受治疗。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:21
msgid "Kamal's wife, travelling with him. Speaks for him when he cannot."
msgstr "Kamal 的妻子，与他同行。在他无法表达时替他发言。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:66
msgid "Malaysia's HIE assembles Kamal's International Patient Summary from his care history: his conditions, his medicines, his allergy. It issues a Verifiable Health Link to it, signs it with a key registered with GDHCN, and puts the QR code in his wallet."
msgstr "马来西亚的 HIE 根据 Kamal 的照护史汇编其国际患者摘要：他的疾病、药物和过敏情况。它为其签发一个可验证健康链接（Verifiable Health Link），用在 GDHCN 注册的密钥对其签名，并将 QR 码放入他的钱包。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:36
msgid "Malaysia's HIE publishes the public keys it signs health documents with to the WHO GDHCN trust network, and shares the national code systems its IPS uses with the WHO Terminology Service (<a0>user scenarios</a0>, first two sections). Nothing about Kamal yet: this is what lets a Saudi clinic trust and read a Malaysian record months later."
msgstr "马来西亚的 HIE 将其用于签名健康文档的公钥发布到世卫组织（WHO）GDHCN 信任网络，并与世卫组织（WHO）术语服务共享其 IPS 所用的国家代码系统（<a0>用户场景</a0>，前两节）。此时尚不涉及 Kamal：正是这一步让沙特的诊所在数月后能够信任并读取马来西亚的记录。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:96
msgid "Not yet consistent here: the <a0>concepts</a0> say the default passcode is the pilgrim's birth date; the Malaysian implementation sets one standard passcode for all its pilgrims for the season."
msgstr "此处尚不一致：<a0>概念</a0>称默认通行码是朝觐者的出生日期；而马来西亚的实现为该季所有朝觐者设置了同一个标准通行码。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:73
msgid "Not yet specified here: no business process for assembling the IPS from the care history."
msgstr "此处尚未规定：没有根据照护史汇编 IPS 的业务流程。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:43
msgid "Not yet specified here: no business process or transaction for publishing keys or terminologies."
msgstr "此处尚未规定：没有发布密钥或术语的业务流程或事务。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:121
msgid "Not yet specified here: no business process, transaction or consent profile for emergency access."
msgstr "此处尚未规定：没有用于紧急访问的业务流程、事务或同意概要文件。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:131
msgid "Not yet specified here: nothing returns the record of care in KSA, or a log of who opened his summary, to Malaysia."
msgstr "此处尚未规定：没有任何机制将他在 KSA 的照护记录或谁打开过他摘要的日志返回给马来西亚。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:109
msgid "Not yet specified here: the summary is in the language it was written in; nothing says how a Saudi clinician reads a summary written in Malay."
msgstr "此处尚未规定：摘要使用其撰写时的语言；没有说明沙特临床医生如何阅读用马来语撰写的摘要。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:59
msgid "Not yet specified here: the two forms the pilgrim fills in, consent-wallet-questionnaire and shl-configure-privacy-settings, are named in the processes but not defined."
msgstr "此处尚未规定：朝觐者填写的两份表单 consent-wallet-questionnaire 和 shl-configure-privacy-settings 在流程中有命名，但未定义。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:24
msgid "Nurse Reem"
msgstr "Nurse Reem"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:91
msgid "Nurse Reem scans the code in the facility's EMR and enters the passcode. The EMR checks the signature with Malaysia's public key, fetched from GDHCN: the record really comes from Malaysia's HIE and has not been changed."
msgstr "Nurse Reem 在医疗机构的 EMR 中扫描该码并输入通行码。EMR 使用从 GDHCN 获取的马来西亚公钥检查签名：该记录确实来自马来西亚的 HIE，且未被更改。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:116
msgid "On the day of Arafat Kamal collapses and is brought in unconscious. Salmah is not with him. Dr Hafiz of the Malaysian medical team gives his Hajj registration number, and the facility reaches his summary through it."
msgstr "在阿拉法特（Arafat）日，Kamal 晕倒，被送来时已失去意识。Salmah 不在他身边。马来西亚医疗队的 Dr Hafiz 提供了他的朝觐（Hajj）登记号，医疗机构通过该号码获取了他的摘要。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:80
msgid "On the second day in Mina, in the heat, Kamal feels dizzy and weak. Salmah brings him to the Hajj health facility. At registration he opens his wallet and shows Nurse Reem the QR code."
msgstr "在米纳（Mina）的第二天，在炎热中，Kamal 感到头晕乏力。Salmah 带他到朝觐（Hajj）医疗机构。登记时，他打开钱包，向 Nurse Reem 出示 QR 码。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:138
msgid "One passcode policy (P4), stated once."
msgstr "一项通行码策略（P4），只陈述一次。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:32
msgid "P0 · Before the season — keys and codes are shared (step A)"
msgstr "P0 · 朝觐季之前——共享密钥和代码（步骤 A）"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:46
msgid "P1 · The health check and the choice to share (step 1)"
msgstr "P1 · 健康检查与共享选择（步骤 1）"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:62
msgid "P2 · His summary is assembled and signed (step 2)"
msgstr "P2 · 汇编并签名他的摘要（步骤 2）"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:76
msgid "P3 · Taken ill in Mina (step 3)"
msgstr "P3 · 在米纳（Mina）患病（步骤 3）"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:87
msgid "P4 · Scanned and checked (step 4, step B)"
msgstr "P4 · 扫描和检查（步骤 4、步骤 B）"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:99
msgid "P5 · His record is read and he is treated (step 5)"
msgstr "P5 · 读取他的记录并对他进行治疗（步骤 5）"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:112
msgid "P6 · When he cannot show the code (Phase 2: break the glass)"
msgstr "P6 · 当他无法出示该码时（第 2 阶段：紧急破例访问）"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:124
msgid "P7 · Back home (after the story the guide tells)"
msgstr "P7 · 回到家中（在本指南所讲述的故事之后）"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:18
msgid "Person"
msgstr "人员"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:110
msgid "Policy question: does Malaysia learn that Kamal's record was opened in KSA, and by whom?"
msgstr "政策问题：马来西亚是否会得知 Kamal 的记录在 KSA 被打开，以及由谁打开？"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:60
msgid "Policy question: is consent given once for the whole Hajj season, per facility, or per encounter — and can Kamal withdraw it while abroad?"
msgstr "政策问题：同意是针对整个朝觐（Hajj）季一次性给出，还是按医疗机构或按就诊给出——Kamal 能否在国外期间撤回同意？"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:132
msgid "Policy question: should the host country send a summary of care back to the home country — and with whose consent?"
msgstr "政策问题：东道国是否宜将照护摘要发回本国——以及需经谁的同意？"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:74
msgid "Policy question: what must the summary contain for a pilgrim — and who decides what is left out?"
msgstr "政策问题：朝觐者的摘要必须包含哪些内容——以及由谁决定省略哪些内容？"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:97
msgid "Policy question: what protection should the passcode give — and is a passcode shared by every pilgrim of a country a passcode at all?"
msgstr "政策问题：通行码应提供什么样的保护——一个国家所有朝觐者共用的通行码还算得上通行码吗？"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:85
msgid "Policy question: what should happen when a pilgrim arrives with no phone, a flat battery, or no QR code?"
msgstr "政策问题：当朝觐者没有手机、手机没电或没有 QR 码时，应如何处理？"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:44
msgid "Policy question: which Malaysian institution signs health documents on behalf of the health sector, and who in KSA decides to accept that signature?"
msgstr "政策问题：哪个马来西亚机构代表卫生部门签名健康文档，以及在 KSA 由谁决定是否接受该签名？"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:122
msgid "Policy question: who may open an unconscious pilgrim's record, on what legal basis, and how is it accounted for afterwards?"
msgstr "政策问题：谁可以打开失去意识的朝觐者的记录，依据什么法律基础，事后如何问责？"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:24
msgid "Registration nurse at a Hajj health facility in Mina."
msgstr "米纳（Mina）一家朝觐（Hajj）医疗机构的登记护士。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:21
msgid "Salmah"
msgstr "Salmah"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:84
msgid "Specified by: business process Clinical Encounter for Unplanned Care (<a0>Business Processes</a0>)."
msgstr "规定于：业务流程“计划外照护临床就诊”（<a0>业务流程</a0>）。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:56
msgid "Specified by: business processes Health Check and Counseling, Explicit Consent on Wallet and Verbal Consent (<a0>Business Processes</a0>); transaction <a1>record consent from wallet</a1>; profile HajjConsent and its examples CONSENT-MYS and CONSENT-KSA (<a2>Artifacts</a2>)."
msgstr "规定于：业务流程“健康检查和咨询，钱包上的明确同意”和“口头同意”（<a0>业务流程</a0>）；事务<a1>从钱包记录同意</a1>；概要文件 HajjConsent 及其示例 CONSENT-MYS 和 CONSENT-KSA（<a2>工件</a2>）。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:120
msgid "Specified by: described in <a0>user scenarios</a0> as a Phase 2 scenario; the <a1>Origin Country Wallet</a1> lets the pilgrim opt in or out of break-the-glass access."
msgstr "规定于：在<a0>用户场景</a0>中作为第 2 阶段场景描述；<a1>来源国钱包</a1>允许朝觐者选择加入或退出紧急破例访问。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:42
msgid "Specified by: the <a0>SMART Trust</a0> framework, by reference."
msgstr "规定于：<a0>SMART Trust</a0> 框架（通过引用）。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:95
msgid "Specified by: the same process (tasks scan QR code, add passcode, verify QR code signature); the receiving steps of the <a0>Malaysian reference implementation</a0>."
msgstr "规定于：同一流程（任务：扫描 QR 码、添加通行码、验证 QR 码签名）；<a0>马来西亚参考实现</a0>的接收步骤。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:71
msgid "Specified by: transaction <a0>issue VHL</a0>; profile HajjIPS and the example My IPS; the folder example My Hajj Pilgrimage Minimal Folder (<a1>Artifacts</a1>)."
msgstr "规定于：事务<a0>签发 VHL</a0>；概要文件 HajjIPS 及示例 My IPS；文件夹示例 My Hajj Pilgrimage Minimal Folder（<a1>工件</a1>）。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:108
msgid "Specified by: transactions <a0>retrieve VHL folder</a0> and <a1>retrieve IPS</a1>; the <a2>Host Country EMR</a2>'s duty to keep a rendered copy; test case View IPS content (<a3>Testing</a3>)."
msgstr "规定于：事务<a0>检索 VHL 文件夹</a0>和<a1>检索 IPS</a1>；<a2>东道国 EMR</a2> 保留渲染副本的义务；测试用例 View IPS content（<a3>测试</a3>）。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:1
msgid "The <a0>user scenarios</a0> of this guide told as one pilgrim's story, step by step along the <a1>overview of key process flows</a1> (the numbered steps 1–5 and A–B of the figure below). Each moment names who takes part, what happens, and what in this guide specifies it, and asks the policy question it raises. Where the guide does not yet specify a moment, the moment says so."
msgstr "将本指南的<a0>用户场景</a0>以一位朝觐者的故事讲述，沿着<a1>关键流程概览</a1>逐步展开（即下图中编号的步骤 1–5 和 A–B）。每个时刻都指明参与者、发生的事情以及本指南中对此作出规定的内容，并提出其引发的政策问题。若本指南尚未规定某个时刻，该时刻会如实说明。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:141
msgid "The data dictionary, decision logic, indicators and functional requirements, which are still placeholders."
msgstr "数据字典、决策逻辑、指标和功能性需求，这些仍是占位内容。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:103
msgid "The EMR follows the link to Malaysia's HIE and retrieves Kamal's summary. Dr Faisal sees the insulin and the penicillin allergy before he treats him for heat exhaustion and low blood sugar. The EMR keeps a rendered copy of the summary with the record of the visit."
msgstr "EMR 沿该链接访问马来西亚的 HIE 并检索 Kamal 的摘要。Dr Faisal 在为他治疗中暑衰竭和低血糖之前，看到了胰岛素和青霉素过敏信息。EMR 将摘要的渲染副本与就诊记录一同保存。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:16
msgid "The people"
msgstr "人物"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:137
msgid "The two pilgrim forms named in P1, and a page for the pilgrim and counsellor actors: their actor files exist but no page includes them."
msgstr "P1 中命名的两份朝觐者表单，以及朝觐者和咨询师参与者的页面：其参与者文件已存在，但没有页面包含它们。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:50
msgid "Three months before Hajj, Kamal has the mandatory pre-Hajj health examination with Dr Aisyah. He is fit to travel. She explains what the Hajj Health Record is, who can see it, and for how long. Kamal agrees on his wallet to share his patient summary with Saudi health workers during Hajj, and sets how the link to it is protected."
msgstr "朝觐（Hajj）前三个月，Kamal 由 Dr Aisyah 进行强制性的朝觐前健康检查。他适合出行。她解释了朝觐健康记录（Hajj Health Record）是什么、谁可以查看以及可查看多久。Kamal 在钱包上同意在朝觐期间与沙特卫生工作者共享其患者摘要，并设置了指向该摘要的链接的保护方式。"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:134
msgid "What the story shows the guide still needs"
msgstr "这个故事揭示本指南仍需补充的内容"

#: input/pagecontent/pilgrim-journey.md:18
msgid "Who they are"
msgstr "他们是谁"
